      "amount": "1 piece",
      "notes": "soaked in water for 30 minutes"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees Fahrenheit.",
    "In a small bowl, whisk together soy sauce, brown sugar, ginger, and black pepper to make the marinade.",
    "Place the pork belly on the cedar plank, leaving a 1-inch border around the pork.",
    "Brush the marinade all over the pork, making sure it is fully coated.",
    "Place the rosemary sprigs on top of the pork.",
    "Roast the pork in the preheated oven for 20 minutes.",
    "Increase the oven temperature to broil and cook for an additional 5 minutes, or until the pork is crispy and golden brown.",
    "Remove the pork from the oven and let it rest for 5 minutes before slicing and serving."
  ],
